    "body": "We understand the importance of offering individualized and personal care because medicine is not a one-size-fits-all service. Our local compounding pharmacy is passionate about working with healthcare providers who want to give their patients personalized prescription medication and treatment options that are tailored to their bodies. So what should you look for when choosing a sterile compounding pharmacy? Keep reading to find out!\nService Area\nHealthcare providers in the state of Texas can rely on our compounding pharmacy services, not just those in the Sulphur Springs area. Additionally, we are expanding our service area and can now serve providers and their patients in Colorado. The ability to ship our medications is a fantastic perk! Plus, providers can easily recommend supplements and wellness products that feature pharmaceutical-grade ingredients backed by science, thanks to our online supplement store!\nAttention To Detail\nOne of the most important things to know about choosing a sterile compounding pharmacy is the attention to detail and ability to work with a variety of patient needs. Our compounding experts create formulas with the utmost care and precision so that patients can have the exact dose their body needs and in a delivery method that works best for them. From liquids that dissolve under the tongue to injections, creams, troches, and more, we work closely with providers to determine the best course of action that improves patient safety and the effectiveness of their prescription medications.\nAdherence to Industry Standards\nThe US Pharmacopeia (USP) is a non-profit organization that has established standards and guidelines regarding the art and science of compounding to promote the continued safety and maintenance of quality standards. We specifically follow chapters 797 and 800, which outline sterile compounding procedures and protocols to ensure a clean, contaminant-free lab.\nWe are also LegitScript certified, which means that we are recognized by important advertising platforms such as Google, Meta, Microsoft, LinkedIn, Visa, Mastercard, and many more. This certification builds trust and lets patients know that LegitScript certified providers operate legally,\nCompounded Medication Options\nCompounding can benefit anyone, from elderly patients requiring a cream or flavored solution for easy administration or to combine multiple medications into one simple dose. Specialized medicine compounding is what we do best, and that includes children’s medications and veterinary prescriptions. We can add flavorings, remove allergens, change the dosage strength or form, and even make medication formulas that have been discontinued or are out of stock. Since we use the main active ingredients to create custom-made medication, patients can save money by using these generic alternatives to name brands.\nAre you interested in working with Cody Drug? Learn more about the types of compounded medications we provide and get in touch with our sterile compounding pharmacy today. Whether your patient could benefit from bioidentical hormone therapy, GLP-1 medications, low-dose naltrexone, topical pain solutions, or wound-healing topicals, we look forward to hearing from you!",
