    "slug": "5-summer-health-tips-you-should-know",
    "title": "5 Summer Health Tips You Should Know",
    "description": "Family vacations, beautiful weather, and summer barbeques– what’s not to love about this time of year? Unfortunately, things like sunburnt skin, heat rash, bug bites, poison ivy, (the list goes on) can get you feeling down!",
    "body": "Family vacations, beautiful weather, and summer barbeques– what’s not to love about this time of year? Unfortunately, things like sunburnt skin, heat rash, bug bites, poison ivy, (the list goes on) can get you feeling down! But we want to share a few summer health tips to help you make the most of the season and hopefully stay happy and healthy.\n1. Go all out with the SPF.\nRubbing on a little sunscreen to your arms and shoulders isn’t going to cut it, especially if you are going to be outside for long periods of time, will be swimming, or are prone to sweating a lot. Protecting your skin from the sun should include the following:\nAt least SPF 30 reapplied every 2 hours\nBe careful when applying spray sunscreen that it actually covers your skin and doesn’t get blown away by the breeze!\nApply sunscreen to your face, neck, ears, hands, and even your scalp if you aren’t wearing a hat. Powder sunscreen is great for not making your hair and scalp oily!\nWear rash guards or breathable clothing with long sleeves whenever possible.\nMake sure your sunglasses have UV protection– your eyes and the skin around them are super sensitive!\n2. Rein in seasonal allergies and pesky bugs.\nCheck out these allergy relief home remedies and be sure to stock up at our independent pharmacy for all your seasonal allergy relief needs– we have OTC products, including sinus support supplements like Texas Cedar Fever Drops. You can also ask us about itching relief creams and other solutions for bug bites, poison ivy rashes, and more!\n3. Hydrate creatively.\nWe get it, no one likes to drink glass after glass of water when fun drinks like soda, juice, sweet tea, and smoothies exist! But the fastest way to heat exhaustion and dehydration is by passing over water for more enticing beverages. Make your water a little more appealing by adding sliced fruit like lemons and limes and fresh herbs such as mint. You should also add more foods with high water content to your diet during the summer– watermelon, cucumbers, celery, tomatoes, strawberries, cantaloupe, pineapple, and zucchini all help your body stay hydrated, but remember, drinking water must always be a top priority!\n4. Try a new seasonal activity or exercise.\nOne of the best summer health tips we have is to go out and try a new outdoor activity or exercise. Not only does exercising provide physical benefits but it also helps with mental health and stress, not to mention the social aspect of exercise! You can bond with your significant other, kids, and other loved ones while doing something fun and exciting! A few examples could be a water aerobics class, frisbee golf, pickleball, hiking or biking a local trail.\n5. Ask us about natural weight loss support options!\nThe summertime is when many people want to look and feel their best for vacation, relaxing by the pool, etc. So why not boost your weight loss efforts with a little help from our compounding pharmacy in Sulphur Springs? We offer natural supplements like fiber, berberine, and probiotics in our Weight Loss Bundle, as well as compounded semaglutide online consultations and prescriptions!\nCurious about natural weight loss medications? Learn more about semaglutide for weight loss and get started implementing these summer health tips into your daily wellness routine!",
